.TH GENESYS-WEB 1 "2026-08-20" "GenESyS" "GenESyS Manual"
.SH NAME
genesys-web \- legacy command alias for the GenESyS HTTP worker
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B genesys-web
.RI [ application-arguments ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B genesys-web
is a compatibility public entry point preserved from the historical
.B genesys-web
Debian package. The canonical application and package are now
.BR genesys-worker (1);
.B genesys-web
remains available as a command alias so scripts and habits from older
installations keep working.
.PP
.B genesys-web
is a small wrapper that execs
.BR /usr/libexec/genesys/genesys-dispatch (8)
with
.BR "--app genesys-web" .
The dispatcher resolves
.B genesys-web
as a compatibility alias for the
.B genesys-worker
application when selecting either the per-user runtime or the
Debian-provided system fallback, and then replaces itself with the selected
executable. All arguments given to
.B genesys-web
are forwarded unchanged.
.PP
.B genesys-web
never performs a network update check.
.SH EXIT STATUS
The exit status of the selected worker executable, or 127 if no valid runtime
could be selected.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR genesys-worker (1)
